<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <title>Psychology of Random Decisions: Why Spin Wheels Work</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Understand decision fatigue, choice overload, and the intuition-reveal effect—why letting a fair spin wheel break deadlocks feels surprisingly freeing." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico?v=1" />
    <meta
      name="keywords"
      content="psychology of random decisions, why random choices feel fair, decision fatigue, choice paralysis, procedural fairness, spin wheel psychology, cognitive bias decision making"
    />
    <meta name="author" content="Harman S., Spin The Wheels Online" />
    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="Why Random Decisions Feel Fair: The Psychology of Letting Chance Choose (2026)"
    />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="A fresh, evidence-informed look at why letting a wheel decide can genuinely beat deliberate choice — for the decisions that don't deserve your full attention."
    />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta
      property="og:url"
      content="https://spinthewheelsonline.com/blogs/psychology-random-decision-making"
    />
    <meta
      property="og:image"
      content="https://spinthewheelsonline.com/eng-yes-no-wheel.webp"
    />
